review_comments:
So I have been reading #10086, I have no idea if @levitte ever solved the problem.

So we have a case here in which AppVeyor fails, but from the discussion over there between @mspncp and @levitte it seems wrong to avoid `_fp` functions because they could cause problems: at least our tests should be built in a way that allows us to test any function of our API (in its Windows version), including the `*_fp` variants that can be problematic if not correctly handled.

@levitte @mspncp suggestions on how to fix the Windows tests now that there is a reproducible event?

@levitte I can see something related to this in the apps/build.info in master, but not in 1.1.1.

How is this problem solved in 1.1.1?

Should this PR fix the Windows build for all the tests or only for this one?
